Assistant: I see the issue. The OptionComponent is being used directly without being wrapped in a React-Select component, which provides the necessary context and styles. Let's fix the preview component by wrapping it in a Select component:

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/OptionComponent-b921da27.tsx">
<change>
<description>Wrap OptionComponent in a Select component with proper context</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import Select from '@calcom/ui/components/form/select/Select';
import { OptionComponent } from '../../../../packages/ui/components/form/select/components';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    option: {
      type: "dropdown",
      value: "option1",
      options: ["option1", "option2", "option3"],
      label: "Select Option",
    },
    isMulti: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Multi Select",
    },
    isSelected: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Selected",
    },
    needsTeamsUpgrade: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Needs Teams Upgrade",
    },
  });

  const options = state.option.options.map(opt => ({
    label: opt,
    value: opt,
    needsTeamsUpgrade: state.needsTeamsUpgrade.value,
  }));

  return (
    <Select
      options={options}
      value={options.find(opt => opt.value === state.option.value)}
      isMulti={state.isMulti.value}
      components={{
        Option: OptionComponent
      }}
      onChange={(newValue) => {
        setState(prev => ({
          ...prev,
          option: {
            ...prev.option,
            value: newValue ? (newValue as any).value : ''
          }
        }));
      }}
    />
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

The changes I made:

1. Imported the Select component from the UI library
2. Created proper options array with the required format
3. Wrapped the OptionComponent in a Select component with proper props
4. Added proper value handling and onChange handler
5. Used the components prop to override the Option component with our custom OptionComponent

This should resolve the "getStyles is not a function" error because now the OptionComponent is being rendered within the proper React-Select context, which provides the necessary styling functions and context.

The error was occurring because we were trying to render the OptionComponent in isolation, but it's meant to be used as a subcomponent of React-Select. By wrapping it in the Select component, we provide all the necessary context and styling functions that the component expects.

